<%= page_heading "API Docs", title: "Dog API Docs - Free JSON API for Dog Breeds, Pictures and Facts" %>
<% content_for :description do %>
  Documentation for the free Dog API: two versions, no key and no sign up.
  V2 follows JSON:API and covers breeds, groups, facts and pictures.
<% end %>
<% breadcrumb_structured_data([["API Docs", docs_path]]) %>

<p>
  There are two versions of the API. The V1, which is the classic one (now deprecated), which uses a custom JSON response.
</p>

<p>
  And V2, which uses JSON API schema as its response format. This version will be widely supported and will be adding new features in the future.
</p>

<ul>
  <li><%= link_to "API V2", api_v2_path %></li>
  <li><%= link_to "API V1 (deprecated)", api_v1_path %></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="mcp">Use it from an AI assistant (MCP)</h2>

<p>
  The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is how AI assistants call outside tools.
  Dog API runs an MCP server, so an assistant can look up breeds and groups,
  fetch dog facts and show a credited picture on its own. Like the rest of the
  API, it needs no key and no sign up.
</p>

<%= render "pages/api_code",
      label: "Server URL",
      id: "mcp-url",
      content: "https://dogapi.dog/mcp" %>

<p>
  It offers six read-only tools: <code>random_dog_facts</code>,
  <code>search_breeds</code>, <code>get_breed</code>, <code>list_groups</code>,
  <code>get_group</code> and <code>random_dog_image</code>.
</p>

<h3>Claude Code</h3>

<%= render "pages/api_code",
      label: "Terminal",
      language: "shell",
      id: "mcp-claude-code",
      content: "claude mcp add --transport http dogapi https://dogapi.dog/mcp" %>

<h3>Claude Desktop and claude.ai</h3>

<p>
  In Settings, under Connectors, add a custom connector named Dog API with
  <code>https://dogapi.dog/mcp</code> as its URL.
</p>

<h3>Cursor</h3>

<%= render "pages/api_code",
      label: ".cursor/mcp.json",
      language: "json",
      id: "mcp-cursor",
      content: api_json({mcpServers: {dogapi: {url: "https://dogapi.dog/mcp"}}}) %>

<h3>VS Code</h3>

<%= render "pages/api_code",
      label: ".vscode/mcp.json",
      language: "json",
      id: "mcp-vscode",
      content: api_json({servers: {dogapi: {type: "http", url: "https://dogapi.dog/mcp"}}}) %>
